Answer:  
Using `try...catch` blocks.

Example:
----------------JS----------------------
async function fetchData() {
  try {
    const response = await fetch('invalid-url');
    const data = await response.json();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error);
  }
}
-----------------------------------------

